      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/Eljaja/BibaVPN\n\n### Category\n\nRust\n\n### Project Title\n\nBibaVPN: a self-hosted Rust tunnel for your VPS\n\n### Project Description\n\nRun a tunnel on your own VPS with a Rust client and server, desktop and Android apps, and encrypted connection invites. It carries SOCKS5 and HTTP CONNECT traffic over TLS + WebSocket. Experimental; not a hosted VPN service.\n\n\n### Highlights\n\nI'm the author of BibaVPN. It brings a Rust tunnel client and server, desktop and Android apps, and encrypted connection invites into one project.\n\n- Your own exit server: deploy it on a VPS you control. The app does not include a hosted VPN service.\n- Encrypted biba:// invites: import connection settings instead of copying server addresses and authentication flags by hand. Share the invite passphrase separately.\n- TCP stream multiplexing and UDP relay over TLS + WebSocket.\n- A local Docker lab lets you explore the project before deploying it on a VPS.\n- The repository includes protocol documentation for readers interested in Rust networking and tunnel design.\n\nBibaVPN is experimental: the protocol may change, it has not had an independent security audit, and iOS traffic forwarding is not implemented. It does not guarantee anonymity or bypassing network filtering.\n\nFeedback on setup, interoperability, and the protocol design is welcome.\n\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\n\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n_No response_",
